==English==
{{wikipedia}}
===Etymology===
From {{etyl|fro}} {{term|collation|lang=fro}}, from {{etyl|la}} {{term|collationem}}, from the participle stem of {{term|conferre||to bring together}}.

===Pronunciation===
*{{a|UK}} {{IPA|/kəˈleɪʃən/}}
* {{rhymes|eɪʃǝn}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|s|-}}

# Bringing together.
## The act of bringing things together and [[compare|comparing]] them; [[collection]], [[comparison]]. {{defdate|from 14th c.}}
## The act of [[collating]] pages or sheets of a book, or from printing etc. {{defdate|from 19th c.}}
# Discussion, light meal.
## {{obsolete}} A [[conference]] or [[consultation]]. {{defdate|14th-17th c.}}
## {{in plural}} The ''Collationes Patrum in Scetica Eremo Commorantium'' by {{w|John Cassian}}, an important ecclesiastical work. (Now usually with capital initial.) {{defdate|from 13th c.}}
## A [[reading]] held from this work, as a regular service in Benedictine [[monastery|monasteries]]. {{defdate|from 14th c.}}
## The light [[meal]] taken by [[monk]]s after this reading service. {{defdate|from 14th c.}}
## Any light [[meal]] or [[snack]]. {{defdate|from 16th c.}}


